    {
      "id": "claim_73754e56271c4f32bb0271cdd7109c2c",
      "statement": "The application configuration is built at startup by reading `app.properties` from the classpath, templating it with a `TemplateProcessor`, and loading the resolved properties into the shared global `Main.p` object. Secret values use `{{ path/to/secret }}` placeholders consumed by the templating step, and a failure here terminates the process with `System.exit(1)`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/Main.java#L41-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3bebd3540b4591f8bda2210d7b7c6b167981a5a6626518ea7af98dbc46a28a9c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9fa02f1e39094cfc8c791b3ac7074227",
      "statement": "`Config.java` is a facade for the OneComm provider's system-property overrides, reading values like `uri_prefix`, `onecomm_service_url`, and `fsp-go.service.*` from Java system properties with hardcoded defaults, and is consumed by OnecommGateway, Fraud, and OnecommPaymentServiceProvider.",
      "evidence": [
        {
